cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you adopt K13, cite the version you adopted."
title: "K13 - Ai General Response Standard"
# CFF 1.2.0 allows only 'dataset' or 'software' at the top level. K13 is a
# standard; 'software' is the closest option the format offers, and it is the
# same choice CITATION.cff makes for AiEDs. GitHub reads only CITATION.cff, so
# this file is for humans and for tools pointed at it directly.
type: software
version: 4.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-27
# Two licenses (see NOTICE): the K13 text is CC BY 4.0; the reference report
# templates and the @randomknights/k13 checker code are Apache 2.0. CFF 1.2.0
# accepts a list of SPDX identifiers here.
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/random-knights/standard
url: https://randomknights.xyz/k13/
abstract: >-
  Thirteen ordered steps for writing an AI response: verify state, record the
  cost, lead with the outcome, flag every roadblock, name the owner action,
  and write one plain, short pass, the quick squeeze, with every figure traced
  and the confidence stated. Version 4 caps the whole answer at a 40-word
  opening and a 400-word body, requires three report tiles rather than twelve,
  and sets a voice rule for the opening. Version 4.1 writes the answer like a
  calm adult explaining to a smart caveman, and carries the humor rules. Model-agnostic. The canonical text is
  K13.md in this repository.
keywords:
  - Ai general response standard
  - quick squeeze
  - open standard
authors:
  - name: "Random Knights, LLC"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-5066-1693"
    city: Roswell
    region: Georgia
    country: US
    website: https://randomknights.xyz
contact:
  - name: "Random Knights, LLC"
    email: knights@rand0m.ai
